<h5>Redirects</h5>
<p>Manage permanent (301) and temporary (302) public URL redirects under <strong>Settings → Redirects</strong>. When a visitor hits a missing path (or an old <code>/p/{slug}</code> / <code>/blog/{slug}</code>), matching active redirects run before the 404 page.</p>
<p>Enter a <strong>from path</strong> like <code>/old-about</code> and a <strong>to</strong> path or absolute URL. Sources under <code>/admin</code>, <code>/api</code>, <code>/serve</code>, and <code>/share</code> are blocked for safety. Hit counts show how often each rule fired.</p>
<p>Admin: <code>/admin/redirects</code> (requires <code>manage_settings</code>)</p>
